  "description": "JUHTUE crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group P 4 n c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C32 H88 Gd9 N16 O50 1-,2(C1 H4 O1),H2 O1,H1 1+. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd1A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd1B (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3B (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd1C (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3C (Gd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.578-5.099 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.61-171.75°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd9(L2)8(μ3-OH)8(μ4-O)2(NO3)8]·2CH3OH·H2O (HL2 = 2-(2-aminoethoxy)ethanol); Anal. C34H90Gd9N16O53. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
